35,2,1,talk,Servas,,The minutes show our senior analysts are gone until autumn. That is a gap.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The ledgers show frozen travel costs, but shipping is up. Staffing is thin.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The spectroscopy suite was idle for eleven weeks. That is a major risk.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The repository is fast now, but breeding colonies cause double the overruns.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The closeout files show catalogue awards last, while mechanism ones stall.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, that idle time is dangerous. We cannot rely on broken tools.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, if the repository is fast, data-heavy projects are safer.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, yes. The animal facility is accredited, but the glasshouse is full.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, so the mechanism-focused ones are risky? That aligns with my data.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, the staffing rolls confirm the technicians are gone. Modelling is staffed.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,We need a project that does not depend on the missing analysts.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,A project using the fast repository and available modelling staff seems wise.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,Avoid anything needing the idle spectroscopy suite or the full glasshouse.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Avoid live breeding colonies. Computation is safer for the schedule.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Catalogue-style awards have a track record of lasting impact.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"So, we look for a data-rich, computation-heavy project.","{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,That sounds like a solid foundation for the decision.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Kenji,,Agreed. We must avoid the infrastructure bottlenecks.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Yes. Let us wait for the candidates to see which fits.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I am ready to evaluate them against these criteria.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
